{"title":"2006 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 22","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2006_CyMO-22.PNG\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/9/9b/2006_CyMO-22.PNG/250px-2006_CyMO-22.PNG\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"250\" height=\"144\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/9/9b/2006_CyMO-22.PNG/375px-2006_CyMO-22.PNG 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/9/9b/2006_CyMO-22.PNG/500px-2006_CyMO-22.PNG 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/0/0c04b99148a42b3ebdb85702618e7f5ec51597fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB\\Gamma \\Delta$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"54\" height=\"13\" /> is rectangular and the points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/6/4b68be08ed973cca73cffb65993b6b493ca8ab1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K,\\Lambda ,M,N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"87\" height=\"16\" /> lie on the sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/5/d65e10100b91763faad3bf091e2e191e50e9dacb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB, B\\Gamma , \\Gamma \\Delta, \\Delta A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"133\" height=\"16\" /> respectively so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/4/6d4206d9dcade646b1be513004984bab4ae98cb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AK}{KB}=\\frac{BL}{L\\Gamma}=\\frac{\\Gamma M}{M\\Delta}=\\frac{\\Delta N}{NA}=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"246\" height=\"38\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/9/459b08d5235f417c69f0cc0c2d473a4739abdb1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> is the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/1/7b122f1689ba54f36205f22f6112320721e70c75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K\\Lambda MN$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"65\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/6/f263b4685391e1f4f3ba204a355cc203a29a0653.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> is the area of the rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/0/0c04b99148a42b3ebdb85702618e7f5ec51597fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB\\Gamma \\Delta$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"54\" height=\"13\" />, the ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/1/401f4ac4886505b593ee907432572b3d312bf78a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{E_1}{E_2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"23\" height=\"40\" /> equals\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/6/3c6f97712242ff01a6ca9d825793424c67837392.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}\\ \\frac{5}{9}\\qquad\\mathrm{(B)}\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\qquad\\mathrm{(C)}\\ \\frac{9}{5}\\qquad\\mathrm{(D)}\\ \\frac{3}{5}\\qquad\\mathrm{(E)}\\ \\text{None of these}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"447\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/9/4b9e03a1fdb0d61f7dea8ebf3c65dec2a1d5552c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = \\Gamma \\Delta = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"113\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/b/81b54a96edf0ebe48292a8fabda6cfcf72c095a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B\\Gamma = A\\Delta = y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"112\" height=\"16\" />. Using the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/f/f3f68d028ef6fe48f36113da99912a90932f18da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KM = \\sqrt{\\frac{x^2}{9} + y^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"140\" height=\"43\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/0/4c0f954024ac3cfc6c2683994613dfbeb144b7ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Lambda N = \\sqrt{x^2 + \\frac{y^2}{9}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"132\" height=\"43\" />. Using the formula <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/2/eb283a0063bb940811701b2a3607c264a07a4cf2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = \\frac{1}{2}d_1d_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"83\" height=\"37\" /> for a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Rhombus\" title=\"Rhombus\">rhombus</a>, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/f/6ffdf072b26772ffb2367e47d6909d3a2ba954d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{\\left(x^2 + \\frac{y^2}{9}\\right)\\left(x^2 + \\frac{y^2}{9}\\right)} = \\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{\\frac{x^4}{9} + \\frac{y^4}{9} + \\frac{82}{81}x^2y^2} = \\frac{\\sqrt{9x^4 + 9y^4 + 82x^2y^2}}{18}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"600\" height=\"53\" />. Thus the ratio is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/5/da5d342d7283b54ece80189247df3810a1b9f3a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt{9x^4 + 9y^4 + 82x^2y^2}}{18xy}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"168\" height=\"43\" />. There is no way we can simplify this further, and in fact we can plug in different values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/4/b6400c6fe3f1ed70e5afd387a9686cdc3fa09531.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"11\" /> to see that the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/7/a07e655cd29678d48f0577dc2f5c5d1dda102c12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{E}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Be careful not to just try a couple of simple examples like <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/0/0c04b99148a42b3ebdb85702618e7f5ec51597fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB\\Gamma \\Delta$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"54\" height=\"13\" /> being a square, where we will get the answer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/1/8f156557a7c96426e1c0934b87e6c77439323195.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5/9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"26\" height=\"18\" />, which is incorrect in general.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; align:center; width:60%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum\" title=\"2006 Cyprus MO/Lyceum\">2006 Cyprus MO, Lyceum</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problems\" title=\"2006 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problems\">Problems</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_21\" title=\"2006 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_23\" title=\"2006 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 23\">Problem 23</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<